{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useRateLimitedValue<TValue, TSelected>(\n   source,\n   options,\n   selector?): [Readonly<ShallowRef<TValue>>, VueRateLimiter<SetValue<TValue>, TSelected>];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/vue-pacer/src/rate-limiter/useRateLimitedValue.ts#L37","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rate-limiter/useRateLimitedValue.ts:37"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Derives a rate-limited value from its current source."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accepts updates while the configured limit has capacity in its fixed or sliding window. Rejected updates are discarded instead of delayed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"return-value","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return value"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns [value, utility]. The value is a readonly shallow ref; read value.value in JavaScript or bind the ref in a template. The source may be a value, a ref, or a getter. The initial value is available immediately. Source changes schedule updates on the existing utility."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-and-ownership","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State and ownership"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The value updates independently of the utility selector. The default utility selection is {}. Pass a selector to subscribe to fields such as executionCount, isPending, or status where the underlying utility exposes them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call during component setup or in an active effect scope. Scope disposal removes watchers and subscriptions and runs utility cleanup.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"source","children":[{"type":"text","value":"source"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ValueSource"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/VuePacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VuePacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/VueRateLimiterOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VueRateLimiterOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SetValue"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"["},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Readonly"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ShallowRef"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">>, "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/VueRateLimiter.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VueRateLimiter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SetValue"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">]"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useRateLimitedValue } from '@tanstack/vue-pacer'\n\n// During component setup:\nconst source = ref('')\nconst [value, utility] = useRateLimitedValue(source, { limit: 3, window: 1000 })\n// Bind value and use utility for controls. Read value.value for the committed value.","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"see","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useRateLimiter"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"return-value","text":"Return value","level":2},{"id":"state-and-ownership","text":"State and ownership","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"source","text":"source","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"see","text":"See","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useRateLimitedValue<TValue, TSelected>(\n   source,\n   options,\n   selector?): [Readonly<ShallowRef<TValue>>, VueRateLimiter<SetValue<TValue>, TSelected>];\n```\n\nDefined in: [rate-limiter/useRateLimitedValue.ts:37](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/vue-pacer/src/rate-limiter/useRateLimitedValue.ts#L37)\n\nDerives a rate-limited value from its current source.\n\nAccepts updates while the configured limit has capacity in its fixed or sliding window. Rejected updates are discarded instead of delayed.\n\n## Return value\n\nReturns [value, utility]. The value is a readonly shallow ref; read value.value in JavaScript or bind the ref in a template. The source may be a value, a ref, or a getter. The initial value is available immediately. Source changes schedule updates on the existing utility.\n\n## State and ownership\n\nThe value updates independently of the utility selector. The default utility selection is {}. Pass a selector to subscribe to fields such as executionCount, isPending, or status where the underlying utility exposes them.\n\nCall during component setup or in an active effect scope. Scope disposal removes watchers and subscriptions and runs utility cleanup.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### source\n\n`ValueSource`\\<`TValue`\\>\n\n### options\n\n[`VuePacerOptions`](../type-aliases/VuePacerOptions.md)\\<[`VueRateLimiterOptions`](../interfaces/VueRateLimiterOptions.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n\\[`Readonly`\\<`ShallowRef`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>, [`VueRateLimiter`](../interfaces/VueRateLimiter.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\]\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useRateLimitedValue } from '@tanstack/vue-pacer'\n\n// During component setup:\nconst source = ref('')\nconst [value, utility] = useRateLimitedValue(source, { limit: 3, window: 1000 })\n// Bind value and use utility for controls. Read value.value for the committed value.\n```\n\n## See\n\nuseRateLimiter\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useRateLimitedValue\ntitle: useRateLimitedValue\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useRateLimitedValue<TValue, TSelected>(\n   source,\n   options,\n   selector?): [Readonly<ShallowRef<TValue>>, VueRateLimiter<SetValue<TValue>, TSelected>];\n```\n\nDefined in: [rate-limiter/useRateLimitedValue.ts:37](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/vue-pacer/src/rate-limiter/useRateLimitedValue.ts#L37)\n\nDerives a rate-limited value from its current source.\n\nAccepts updates while the configured limit has capacity in its fixed or sliding window. Rejected updates are discarded instead of delayed.\n\n## Return value\n\nReturns [value, utility]. The value is a readonly shallow ref; read value.value in JavaScript or bind the ref in a template. The source may be a value, a ref, or a getter. The initial value is available immediately. Source changes schedule updates on the existing utility.\n\n## State and ownership\n\nThe value updates independently of the utility selector. The default utility selection is {}. Pass a selector to subscribe to fields such as executionCount, isPending, or status where the underlying utility exposes them.\n\nCall during component setup or in an active effect scope. Scope disposal removes watchers and subscriptions and runs utility cleanup.\nOptions accept an object with top-level getters or an options factory. Function-valued core options remain callbacks. Local options override provider defaults without replacing the utility or its pending work.\nonUnmount replaces default cleanup and receives the utility instance. A custom callback must perform every needed cancel, stop, or abort action.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### source\n\n`ValueSource`\\<`TValue`\\>\n\n### options\n\n[`VuePacerOptions`](../type-aliases/VuePacerOptions.md)\\<[`VueRateLimiterOptions`](../interfaces/VueRateLimiterOptions.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n\\[`Readonly`\\<`ShallowRef`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>, [`VueRateLimiter`](../interfaces/VueRateLimiter.md)\\<`SetValue`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\]\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useRateLimitedValue } from '@tanstack/vue-pacer'\n\n// During component setup:\nconst source = ref('')\nconst [value, utility] = useRateLimitedValue(source, { limit: 3, window: 1000 })\n// Bind value and use utility for controls. Read value.value for the committed value.\n```\n\n## See\n\nuseRateLimiter\n"}
